(version 1)

# SK6812 MINI-E is reverse-mounted: the LED body sits in its own cutout and the
# pads necessarily end ~0.05-0.1 mm from that cutout. Relax edge clearance ONLY
# between an LED's pads and the Edge.Cuts cutout of an LED footprint. Everything
# else (tracks, other footprints, the board outline) keeps the global 0.25 mm.
# Fab note: this is a waived manufacturing risk, not a fix - the router may nick
# pad copper at the cutout. Keep the pads; they still solder fine if trimmed.
(rule "SK6812 MINI-E pads to own cutout"
	(constraint edge_clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.memberOfFootprint('LED*') && B.Layer == 'Edge.Cuts' && B.memberOfFootprint('LED*')"))
